    "narrative": "The internal model for Ghost Ride the WHIP reflects a thin slate today, forcing a heavy reliance on **Brice Turang** to anchor the infield production. While his 46.03 efficiency score sits in the \"Marginal\" bucket, he remains our primary engine due to his speed profile in a landscape where stolen bases are at a premium. Facing Pivetta (3.17 xERA), **Brice Turang** faces a challenge, but his promotion to the #4 spot in the order provides a vital cushion to his projection, compensating for the elite arm work he faces today. We are effectively playing for his floor, as the optimizer has benched the remainder of our core assets like **Corbin Carroll**, **Josh Naylor**, and **James Wood** due to the scheduled off-day, which essentially resets our roster health for the upcoming stretch.\n\nThe bench decisions today were largely dictated by the league-wide schedule, leaving us without the services of **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Jose Caballero**, and **Mickey Moniak**, who would have otherwise challenged for higher-leverage slots. **Tyler Soderstrom** remains a non-factor on the IL, limiting our depth in the catching and power-hitting roles. We are currently navigating a total lack of positional depth, meaning players like **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **Trevor Story** are relegated to the pine alongside **Isaac Paredes** and **Gabriel Moreno**. The absence of **Max Muncy**, **Moises Ballesteros**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Cole Young**, **Griffin Conine**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Travis Bazzana** emphasizes that today is a \"preservation\" day for our game caps. If the weather reports or late-scratch rumors materialize for **Brice Turang**, we are effectively punting the scoring categories until tomorrow's full slate.",
